#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:5
#: f8ae0b7c0fd54077952346c368dd1718
msgid "Rebasing: keeping your code up to date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:10
#: 3b5f951ac21f43759f76793752d3c562
msgid "As you develop, ArduPilot's master  branch is likely to be updated with \"commits\" from other developers. You should `keep your local branches and fork up to date <http://robots.thoughtbot.com/keeping-a-github-fork-updated>`__ so that you are working with the latest code and to make it easier for maintainers to eventually merge your changes to ArduPilot's master branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:14
#: 1c5737624c7d441a9597e51af695df10
msgid "In particular it is best to keep your local repo and forked repo's master branches up-to-date with ArduPilot's master branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:16
#: 2f2cb74c4eb2421689675c7c3369e2aa
msgid "\"Rebasing\" allows you to update a branch from ArduPilot's master branch and then re-apply any changes you may have made to the branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:20
#: 026312863efa4c69b20d7c18b61d67d5
msgid "The following commands can be entered directly into a Linux/OSX terminal or if using Windows, launch the \"Git Shell\" or \"Git Bash\" utility that should already be :ref:`installed <git-install>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:23
#: 4d21bac6f0bb4929a7550ccce2038ed1
msgid "Navigate to your ardupilot git repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:29
#: 1862a2acb05d4d8f86f741ef6591ed41
msgid "Starting from here we will assume that you want to rebase your topic-branch on ArduPilot master branch. This process is the same for the master branch, just replace topic-branch with master. Ensure you are looking at your master branch or the branch that you want to rebase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:36
#: 0a607c3a7ff14191b1a375cd37690bc8
msgid "If you want to create a new branch to work on which you would like to rebase on top of the ArduPilot master branch,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:43
#: 2a551b61f52b49bca51431601c27f95d
msgid "Ensure your repository is connected to the upstream repository you forked from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:50
#: 7e97763656ff44ab902855963c700e20
msgid "Fetch changes from the upstream repository (this simply downloads changes into a local cache, it will not overwrite or modify your changes in any way). If you are rebasing your branch on your own fork's master branch, replace upstream with origin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:58
#: ded445429d3245889f98c6c94ff82fa2
msgid "Rebase your current branch from the upstream's master branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:64
#: fadd0312d4474bc38d5b222d98051f25
msgid "Initialize and update your local repo's submodules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:70
#: 8a650bbb38274e3c81b02efc08a67c01
msgid "Check that the rebase was successful. Using cmdline (``git log --oneline --decorate --all --graph`` , type q to exit) or a GUI tool like gitk, sourcetree, etc. Your commits should appear on top of ArduPilot master latest commit, like show on previous picture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:72
#: 0cb605a544ef44c58312de5e6c2dc9a7
msgid "Now push the updated branch to your github repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:80
#: d278d09fde1f4bc5bf47c9ccf330e48f
msgid "When things go wrong"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:82
#: e4b04d5155834db78d0641924ff9c6e7
msgid "The rebase step (step 5) above may fail for a few reasons:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:84
#: 5a3e920f2129411cad792decd71ab1f3
msgid "there are uncommitted changes to files in your local repo's branch.  Stage and commit these changes and then try again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:85
#: e6f3c3c125f6499288a20ff7d2b06bdf
msgid "there are merge conflicts meaning that another developer has changed the same lines of code as your new commits have changed.  There are two choices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:87
#: bb48ec9ea9464648b337f20d0e628d3f
msgid "abort the rebase which will restore your branch to how it was before you began the rebase, ``git rebase --abort``.  If you are happy to throw away your new commits in your local repo's branch you can \"reset\" your branch so that it looks exactly like upstream master using ``git reset --hard upstream/master``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:88
#: bd0459913eaf404f929a9502ab4613b5
msgid "user a merge tool like `TortoiseGit <https://tortoisegit.org/>`__ to resolve the mergeconflict and then continue with the rebase using ``git rebase --continue``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-rebase.rst:90
#: 1f175941a6904415b58a32d9c80b6c39
msgid "The submodule update (step 6) occasionally fails if new submodules have been added.  ``git submodule init`` usually resolves this."
msgstr ""

